WEBVTT

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:11.190
Crap!

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.700
What the hell?!

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.700
<b>Switching to Autopilot</b>

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.440
Oscar II, the out-of-control vehicle has 
been identified as a tanker truck.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.590
It's currently headed toward Tokyo 
on the Toumei Expressway,

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.460
around the 14.3-kilometer marker.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.150
Its cargo consists of gasoline and lighter fluid.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.000
To prevent any accidents, exercise utmost 
caution when stopping the vehicle.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.420
Oscar II, roger that.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.060
I-I'm gonna hit it!

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.450
Boss, an unidentified flying object is 
approaching from twelve o'clock.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.310
It may be a Willwear.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:46.020
Huh?

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.320
Crap, I might not make it...

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.930
Oscar I? Thank God...

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:57.940
Huh?

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.490
A civilian?

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.620
Um, thank you for your cooperation.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.110
What's your division?

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.360
Hey!

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.080
Come on, at least tell me your name!

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.640
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:24.320
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:30.020
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.010
<b>File 8: Ulti-maid-ronde</b>

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.170
Oscar IV, equip inner unit.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:49.340
Vitals, all green.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:50.320
All green.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.230
All green, lock.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:59.240
Inner unit, begin output.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.450
Oscar IV, set Koutetsujin Nanakamado Unit.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.200
Oscar VI on scene.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.220
It looks like a boy's been left behind back here.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.150
This is built like a safety deposit box...

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:40.180
Hmph, this is nothing.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.410
That's the Wear from yesterday.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:47.560
How could a civilian manage to get in,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.170
when my Fine Familia couldn't?

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:54.050
That...

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.870
That can't possibly be a mass-market model.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.710
Then what is it?

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:07.030
"The police's new guardian angel?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.100
The Ulti-maid at work."

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.180
There goes the press, 
randomly naming things again.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.230
Looks like the name came from a 
celebrity blog this time, though.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:21.150
<b>The Police's New Guardian Angel? 
The Ulti-maid at Work</b>

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.030
"With the Third Mobile Assault Unit 9's creation,

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.150
Unit 8 is already yesterday's news."

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.740
"The Ulti-maid is sick."

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.520
"The Ulti-maid is way too cool."

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:28.520
"Thirty-four Ulti-maid fan clubs born nationwide"?

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.690
It's all the rage.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.580
I heard there will even be 
Ulti-maid rice crackers now.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.210
Why does it get a fan club, and we don't?

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:41.680
Maybe because we're a little 
rough around the edges?

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:42.920
I am not!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.650
Well, I can see why, though.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.680
Its capabilities are pretty amazing.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.060
I kind of wish I could dismantle and examine it.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.390
Why not ask the Council about it?

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:56.850
Well, it's not from any of 
the affiliate manufacturers.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.250
Really?

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.780
But the whole point is to keep 
the Council in the loop,

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.570
even if you're secretly developing one.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:05.650
Maybe some university made 
one without telling anyone?

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:08.620
Or maybe the police really are behind it?

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.870
I asked the brass, but they said 
they hadn't heard of it.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.620
They were pretty shocked, so I think 
they were telling the truth.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.230
Still, if a Wear like that 
goes into mass production,

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:21.340
we'll have to reconsider Unit 8's equipment.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.910
I doubt a division dubbed "the garbage men"

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:25.820
will get a bigger slice of the budget.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:28.310
There might not even be any use for us anymore.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:32.970
Huh? Hey, don't all clam up on that!

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.310
Well...

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.480
Yeah.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.110
Why are you following me?

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:50.010
Oh, I forgot to tell you earlier,

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:52.450
but I'll be waiting for you tomorrow at 6 PM,

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.910
at Okamoto Tarou in Shibuya's Keiou.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.140
What for?

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:58.630
I don't remember agreeing to meet up with you.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:05:59.710
It's for drinks.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.440
I had someone cancel on me,

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.290
so I'll include you in the fun.

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.170
Drinks? Now, of all times?

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.330
Is that so wrong?

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:09.390
We were just talking about the Ulti-maid.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.040
So what?

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.880
It's not our enemy or anything.

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:15.810
I'd even call it a dependable 
ally that has our backs.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:20.620
That stuff about there being no 
use for us anymore is just talk.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:23.260
At worst, we'd just be 
reassigned somewhere else.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.610
For once, you have a point.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.720
Right? So let's go for drinks.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.570
That's where you lose me.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.180
Well, my friend's organizing it,

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:34.990
and he said some real babes are coming...

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:40.420
There's nothing less credible than the 
promise of babes at a drinking party.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.590
You don't have to come if you don't want.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:46.500
But one of them does look 
a lot like Baba Micchii, I hear.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.530
Baba Micchii...

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:54.970
Asami-chan, are you free tomorrow?

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.850
Yeah, I have nothing really going on.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.630
Why do you ask?

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:01.650
Oh, there's going to be a great event tomorrow!

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:04.470
<i>That's what was supposed to happen, anyway.</i>

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.520
Why is it these two?

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.530
Why is it these two?

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.360
My friend said he was having

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:14.640
a drinking party, and invited me.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.850
Well, mine, too.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:20.330
And said organizer also canceled last-minute?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.250
The girl he was supposed 
to bring isn't here, either.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.740
So Baba Micchii won't be here, either?

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:29.210
Why is that my fault?

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.480
Who's this Baba Micchii?

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:32.300
No idea.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:35.920
And here I'd chosen Italian clothing

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.310
to match the Italian food today.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.540
Souichirou?

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:42.100
We've reserved the entire place today— Hey!

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.840
Whoa, major babe!

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:45.920
Don't be rude, Kuroki-san!

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.370
No way...

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.030
What a coincidence.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:54.350
I was asked to come here for Mayumi, 
since she had to cancel.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:56.690
Oh, okay...

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:58.080
So Mayumi asked you.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:58.840
Yes.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.540
So this "Mayumi" is the Baba Micchii lookalike?

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.250
Just who is Baba Micchii?

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.360
It's nice to meet you all. I'm—

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:08.750
Oh!

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.740
Ooshikouchi Miho-san?

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.230
Huh? Wait, you know each other?

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:18.050
No, but I've seen her several times 
in magazines and on TV.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.920
Right! You've been on magazine covers!

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:23.350
Yes, a rising star in the USDF.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.570
USDF?

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.440
Oh! You were at the jumbo jet incident!

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:29.150
Guess we won't need introductions.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:29.860
Right!

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.070
Still, I didn't expect to see

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.450
Souichirou in a place like this.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:38.990
If I remember right, you wore that 
brand on our first date, too.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.410
D-Did I?

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.630
What's this about a first date?

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.370
Sena Souichirou is my ex.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.820
Huh?!

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:49.130
To be precise, my ex-ex-ex-ex-boyfriend, I think.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:57.810
I have to say, I'm really surprised

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:01.560
to learn that Ooshikouchi-san 
and Sena-san used to date!

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:02.930
You can call me Miho.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.520
May I ask a question?

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:10.490
Why would a lady like you be 
with a blockhead like Sena?

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:12.020
Who're you calling a blockhead?

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:16.240
We were in the same year at the Defense Academy.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.460
The same year?

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:20.130
Souichirou was the star.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.040
After me, that is.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:25.700
But in marksmanship, he was my better.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.360
He shot me through. Right here.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:34.880
It's the same at Unit 8. Sena's the star.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.510
But I wonder...

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.790
Maybe the better fit for you

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.970
would be someone like me!

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.970
Since when are you a better choice than me?

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:47.140
Oh, you remembered I don't like tomatoes?

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.070
That makes me happy.

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:50.060
Oh, well...

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:53.460
Um, why did you break up?

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.190
Sorry, but I should get going—

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.310
Yeah, go home, blockhead.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.570
You don't have to go, Souichirou.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:01.990
This wine you picked is excellent.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:03.670
It pairs well with rabbit.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:07.240
This white wine reflects your deep 
knowledge of Italian wines, as well.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.080
That's why we broke up.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.780
He always strives for perfection,

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:15.100
and has the same expectations of his date.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.170
That's Souichirou's shortcoming.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:19.110
Even for dates,

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:22.740
he'd send a minute-by-minute breakdown 
of the schedule the day before.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.260
And he'd tell me what to wear.

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:27.570
He'd ask me to walk at a certain speed, too.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:28.930
That'd be tiring.

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:29.850
True.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.430
I totally get it!

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:33.650
He makes me tired every day, as well.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.060
H-Hey!

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:42.780
Sena-kun, a building-demolition heavy machinery 
device has gone berserk in Tachikawa City.

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:44.950
There are already several casualties.

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.700
We couldn't reach Kuroki-kun, 
so we hoped to catch you, at least.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:51.760
You idiot!

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:55.070
Please stay away! It's dangerous!

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:55.070
Hey, where's backup?

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:00.710
Yes, that's right.

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:02.080
We think it's a malfunction.

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:04.970
We've had difficulty even getting 
close enough to turn it off.

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:08.640
Based on your blood alcohol levels,

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.070
we can't clear you two for duty.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:12.940
Really?

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.820
Sorry.

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:19.550
I'll be Sena-san's backup, 
now that he's gone ahead.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:20.570
Hang on.

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:23.280
I'm detecting an unidentified flying object.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.950
Unidentified...

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:26.280
Wait!

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.710
Get back! Please get back! It's dangerous!

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.460
Well, it's sure not holding back.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:33.590
All right...

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:36.250
I can't predict its movement!

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:43.970
U-Ulti-maid...

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:45.110
I thought so.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.170
You haven't changed.

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:59.810
You're still slow to adapt in 
unpredictable situations.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:00.790
It can't be...

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:03.210
I see, it was the Defense Ministry's...

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:06.280
It appears it was the USDF's prototype.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:11.770
There were two times in my life that 
I was utterly taken by surprise.

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:15.350
The first was during my college years, when I...

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:18.250
No, when you agreed to my request.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:21.120
The second was when I learned you're Ulti-maid.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.200
To be precise, it's called "Senbukai."

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:24.820
Why not?

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.490
You need some surprises in life.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:31.890
So you don't know anything on 
your end, either, Inagi-kun?

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:33.450
Nothing specific.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.920
It's true that the Defense 
Ministry seeks to expand

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:41.210
USDF jurisdiction by gaining 
Willwear sole-usage rights...

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:43.820
But that runs counter to the 
Basel Conference's decision.

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:46.760
Right, it opposes the ACTIVE project that allows

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.660
the police to arm themselves with Willwears.

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:52.110
But that's the direction this nation's headed in.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.250
Either way, it's out of your control.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:13:00.380
You should just keep doing what 
you've always done.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.710
Yeah, we're adults here.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:06.600
There were two things in my life 
that surprised me, as well.

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:09.640
The first was when you asked me out.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:12.890
The second was when you dumped me.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.200
That's a misunderstanding.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:16.480
I suppose I should thank you

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.440
for letting me pretend I was 
the one who dumped you

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:21.780
in front of your curious group of friends.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.730
Like I said, it's not as if I dumped you.

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:25.280
Yeah, right.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.780
You stopped responding to my messages.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:30.570
You were trying to let it fizzle out, weren't you?

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:31.630
How pathetic.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:34.450
You didn't even have the guts to tell me it was off.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:39.580
You're the only stain on my perfect life.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:42.860
It's not as if I even liked you, you know.

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:46.690
You were just so desperate to win 
me over that I felt sorry for you.

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:48.190
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.140
How dare you dump me?

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:53.620
You're far inferior to me.

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:57.410
I am a USDF elite and a Wear-prototype pilot.

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.940
You're in Unit 8, a division scorned as garbage men.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:13:59.940
Stop it!

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:02.490
What did you say?

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.330
You can insult me all you want.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.450
But don't badmouth Unit 8!

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:12.700
That look suits you much more.

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:20.080
By the way, are you free tomorrow?

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.270
It isn't right?

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:31.550
Yeah, I think something isn't right between us.

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.890
Why are we meeting like this after we broke up?

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:36.290
You're right.

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:38.390
Then do you want to get back together?

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:41.840
And this time, I'll be the one who dumps you.

00:14:42.970 --> 00:14:46.150
Then maybe the stain on my life will disappear.

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:47.770
That's so pointless.

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:50.280
I know. Don't take that seriously.

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:56.210
I'm just meeting with you to pass
the time, and nothing more.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:57.720
Who'd go out with you?

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.500
That's ridiculous.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:01.630
Um...

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:06.680
You idiot, you idiot, you idiot, you idiot!

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:19.000
We've just received the next 
message from the perp.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:22.480
He's rigged a timed explosive in an 
Oomiya building under construction.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:24.980
The bomb's been confirmed.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:27.150
We can probably get good data from this.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:31.150
Dealing with this will serve as 
Senbukai's public announcement.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.720
I heard the press will be involved.

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:36.210
We're counting on you, 
First Lieutenant Ooshikouchi.

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:36.780
Yes, sir!

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:40.560
The brass is telling us to 
cooperate with the USDF.

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:41.310
Sena-kun...

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:41.660
Here.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.090
We also have our reputation to maintain,

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:48.090
but when public safety is at stake, 
we can't be found lacking.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:49.560
I'm counting on you.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:50.590
Understood.

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:00.100
You're just in the way, Souichirou.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.080
Go home.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:02.540
We're both here on orders.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:03.850
I don't care.

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:07.140
Sure, you were impressive 
when we were students.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.770
But I've gained experience at Unit 8.

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:12.110
Don't think I'm the same man as back then.

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:13.370
Oh?

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:15.660
Then show me what you're capable of.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.120
The bomb's in the right-hand room

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:29.090
<b>Scan Mode 
IR Scan</b>

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:21.610
after this corridor.

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:23.830
Laser sensors?

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:26.530
That's right. Hitting a laser will detonate

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:29.090
the bomb, timer or no timer.

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:30.360
Listen.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.430
If we fail this mission,

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:34.930
we'll both be blasted to smithereens 
along with this building.

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:36.720
Oh, how fun.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:39.010
So I want to apologize.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.410
What are you talking about?

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:43.940
The movie we saw on our first date... 
I made the wrong choice.

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:45.280
I knew that.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:47.120
You were bored.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:48.260
I'm sorry.

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:49.940
That ass! He's showing off?

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:49.470
Yeah.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:52.380
Watching someone else's romance is pointless.

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:53.150
No, he just forgot he's on the general comms.

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:53.150
Right.

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:54.680
I'm sorry.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:57.830
Nice...

00:16:57.830 --> 00:16:59.580
Very nice, Souichirou.

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:00.380
Huh?

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.930
Apologize to me more!

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:02.940
Uh, okay...

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:04.980
Does she have a weird fetish or something?

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:06.860
I'd like to apologize for making you eat tomatoes.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:07.070
Um, shouldn't we stop listening?

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:09.040
But we'll lose track of what's going on.

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:09.040
That's right! Keep going!

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:12.050
When we went to Grand Maison for your birthday,

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:15.070
I was so nervous, I neglected proper etiquette

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:16.540
and took the seat of honor.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:17.610
Forgive me.

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:20.100
Yes! That was so humiliating!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.850
Come on, apologize more!

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:24.480
More! More!

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:30.390
What's with this guy? Is he toying with us?

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:30.940
Be careful.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:33.000
I'm detecting explosives.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.330
I see...

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.070
If it hits the floor, it goes boom.

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:39.240
This reminds me of when we met up again.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.910
When the jumbo jet was in a holding pattern?

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:42.900
Hey, hey!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.250
They just keep coming.

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:48.970
Keep it together, Souichirou!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:56.300
They've stopped?

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:58.250
Hurry up! There's no time left!

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.180
R-Right.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.660
Could the perp be

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:03.610
trying to collect Willwear data?

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:08.940
This is...

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:11.880
The entire floor's a detonator?

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.240
Equipped with a heat sensor, too.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.690
I guess they can't fly, then.

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:19.200
What now?

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:23.400
This is no time for us to compete.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.000
Go, Souichirou. I'll keep you stable.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:26.860
Got it.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:29.580
Your split-second decision-making 
is as good as ever.

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:34.390
I guess the biggest apology I have to make to you

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:35.460
is for me.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.730
I want to apologize for myself.

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:40.620
Shut up, Souichirou.

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:43.730
I told you this before, but I didn't dump you.

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:45.860
You were always perfect.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:49.180
That's why I wanted to be perfect, too.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.970
I said shut up!

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:52.630
Huh? What?

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:54.440
But I couldn't be.

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:57.900
No matter how hard I tried, 
I couldn't be perfect for you.

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.570
I couldn't stand that about myself.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:02.870
I'm not worthy of you.

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:04.310
That's why I...

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:05.380
I...

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:09.100
Bomb disarmed.

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:13.880
Now we just need to find this joker.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.000
Wh-What?

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:18.590
M-Miho, are you trying to kill me?

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:21.620
No! Senbukai's acting without my control!

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:23.510
This is...

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:25.470
First Lieutenant Ooshikouchi?

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:26.430
What's going on?

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.850
Ulti-maid's IFF seems to be

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:31.640
defining Sena-san as an enemy target.

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:34.580
Senbukai may have malfunctioned

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.360
due to interference.

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:38.570
Retrieve Senbukai stat!

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.530
Don't let Unit 8 get their hands on it!

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:44.020
Do something, Souichirou!

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:45.620
Stop Senbukai!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.700
Oscar I, fire at the Ulti-maid's feet.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.830
Shoot, Souichirou!

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:54.750
Forgive me.

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:01.970
USDF's strong...

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:05.720
Like I said, we need you to stop your Wear now!

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:07.380
Are you giving us orders?

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:09.630
This is not the time to be petty!

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:13.320
Souichirou, I want to apologize to you, too.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.440
It's a lie that you were a stain on my life!

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:17.740
I... I...

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:19.280
Thank you, Miho.

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:22.520
The truth is, I...

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:23.600
I...

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:25.050
Miho, I...

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:26.370
I...

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.410
The sublimation module! Get out, Oscar I!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.160
Run!

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.120
Sena! Can you hear us, Sena?!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:37.710
Why does your voice have to 
be the last thing I hear?

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.490
Oh, I guess this is my punishment...

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.010
USDF?

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:48.640
I didn't expect them to actually come!

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:02.270
Miho!

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:03.850
M-Miho!

00:21:03.850 --> 00:21:05.450
Souichirou...

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:10.200
I was right! I should let her know.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:11.240
President?

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:13.120
What are you doing?

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:15.040
Good timing, Hinata-kun.

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.440
Isn't your sister a member of the police force?

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:18.250
Oh, yes.

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:20.640
I need to talk to her 
about something important.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:22.710
Would she know someone high up?

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:27.010
Well, she's in the Community Safety Division...

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:29.550
Oh, I guess it'd be hard, then.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:35.770
<i>Next in the news, the subject of several 
recent eyewitness reports, the so-called...</i>

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:36.790
Funasaka-san...

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:39.330
Who's Baba Micchii?

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.090
Ah, that's...

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:41.640
Oh.

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:44.400
She was a handful,

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.300
but I do feel bad for her.

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:46.930
Yeah.

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:49.930
<i>There are rumors that you're Ulti-maid.</i>

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:54.870
<b>Is the pilot a beautiful SDF officer? 
Is the Ulti-maid an SDF Unit?</b>

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:53.050
<i>Is the Ulti-maid really under 
the Defense Ministry?</i>

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:54.870
<i>No comment.</i>

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:57.330
<i>Don't you think pleading 
ignorance is irresponsible?</i>

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:59.790
<i>With the Ulti-maid's feats being so public, 
how can you know nothing of it?</i>

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:00.860
Sena-san?

00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:04.130
Could you come with me 
to the manufacturer's car?

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:04.870
Okay.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:12.430
"The truth is," huh?

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:51.990
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:52.110
Ohakonyapachininko!

00:23:51.990 --> 00:24:04.990
File 9: In the Name of Logos

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:52.840
It's Liko.

00:23:52.840 --> 00:23:55.390
There are rumors that Logos will finally 
make its move in the next episode.

00:23:55.390 --> 00:23:58.050
I searched for the truth on 
the director's computer!

00:23:58.050 --> 00:24:00.420
I learned there will be betrayal 
and idiots everywhere.

00:24:00.420 --> 00:24:02.080
There will be no future for any of them.

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:04.010
Next time, "In the Name of Logos."

00:24:04.010 --> 00:24:04.830
Please watch!
